06:21.000 --> 06:23.800
Now, something worth noting about the vif directive,

06:23.800 --> 06:27.600
though, is that when you use the vif directive, what view

06:27.600 --> 06:33.120
is actually doing is, if we take a look here,

06:33.120 --> 06:36.480
is that the UL that you have here for the else condition

06:36.480 --> 06:39.040
does not even exist on the DOM.

06:39.040 --> 06:42.520
So basically, the elements are being destroyed and recreated

06:42.520 --> 06:44.160
each time you toggle that.

06:44.160 --> 06:46.520
So as you can see here now, if we take a look at the app,

06:46.520 --> 06:48.880
you'll notice here that the UL is president,

06:48.880 --> 06:51.080
that the p tag is gone.

06:51.080 --> 06:54.660
And so this is contrary to another directive

06:54.660 --> 06:57.560
that you will see in view called v-show, which is,

06:57.560 --> 06:59.680
I'll say, it's less popular cousin.

06:59.680 --> 07:01.360
And that's because what v-show does

07:01.360 --> 07:05.280
is it toggles the visibility of the element via CSS.

07:05.280 --> 07:07.240
And so the reason you want those two different approaches

07:07.240 --> 07:12.000
is because there are times where it might be a performance

07:12.000 --> 07:15.880
bottleneck of destroying a list of thousands of items

07:15.880 --> 07:17.920
and then having the DOM recreated every time someone

07:17.920 --> 07:19.000
toggles it on and off.

07:19.000 --> 07:21.040
And you might just want to show or hide it.

07:21.040 --> 07:23.200
So that's where v-show, v-hide could be very useful

07:23.200 --> 07:24.360
in those regards.

07:24.360 --> 07:29.920
So once again, the idea here, building on what we know

07:29.920 --> 07:31.680
and trying to make it easy for us to do

07:31.680 --> 07:33.000
the right performance optimization.

07:33.120 --> 07:35.320
That's a trade-off to consider when using v-f.

07:35.320 --> 07:37.240
But again, I would say 95% of the time,

07:37.240 --> 07:38.480
that is what you want to use.

07:38.480 --> 07:41.000
But the moment you start thinking, oh, users

07:41.000 --> 07:42.360
are going to be toggling this a lot,

07:42.360 --> 07:46.840
and it might be expensive to destroy it, reach out for v-show.

